I'm not so sure about that.

Remember that license for 3.2.2 did have the sentence "Stated plainly:
You are prohibited by the terms of this License Agreement from using
NetHack for gainful purposes. [...]"

But in 3.3.0 this was removed.


I'd ask the DevTeam themselves what they think about the whole idea:
http://www.nethack.org/common/contact.html


IANAL but I would say that the paragraph 2c "[...] you may at your option
offer warranty protection in exchange for a fee." already offers an
option for a commercial distribution.


I see an other problem. There are only two options if you want to
distribute NetHack or derivative of it in executable form. One is to
accompany the executable with the source code (which I think isn't
possible for a XBox game in a way that the user could use the source
code) or including information how to get it from "an appropriate
archive site". But the last option is only allowed for non-commercial
distribution.

So how could one comply? (without asking the DevTeam for permission)


This last bit is of course a remnant of the times where net access
wasn't omnipresent.

